-- id: exp6804-priority-arbiter-ab
-  title: Priority arbiter versus flat reject-and-retry A/B
-  track: verification
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 180
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.08.594
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6804_priority_arbiter_ab.json
-  gated_on:
-    - upstream: exp6803-sota-operational-handoff-corpus
-      artifact_field: operational_handoff_corpus_ready
-      op: '=='
-      value: true
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6803 freezes authentic structured proposals from all three mandated model families. xTRUCE
-    (arXiv:2608.28532) suggests that hard limits, binding rules, and relaxable targets need an
-    explicit priority order plus conflict certificates. Compare that design with a flat
-    reject-and-retry control. Reuse frozen outputs. Do not invoke an LLM or tune on held outcomes.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6802_operational_obligation_automaton_v2.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6803_sota_operational_handoff_corpus.json
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/agentic/arc_trajectory_supervisor.py
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/verify/constraint.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/agentic-verification/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py
-
-    TASK:
-    Build a deterministic priority arbiter over the frozen proposal sets and compare it with a flat
-    reject-and-retry control at matched proposal, check, and wall budgets. The exact transition
-    simulator remains outside both arms. Hard violations must always be rejected.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require operational_handoff_corpus_ready=true, every planned model and arm,
-       raw-byte hashes, complete proposal sets, and the Exp6802 compiler. On failure write a
-       complete_blocked_priority_arbiter_ab artifact with gate_check_summary and stop.
-    1. Add or extend a REQ-* priority-arbitration contract. Write tests first for lexicographic
-       dominance, stable tie breaking, no legal candidate, conflict certificates, and budget parity.
-    2. Freeze development and held scenario IDs. Use development rows only for public constants.
-       The priority arm minimizes hard violations, then binding shortfall in declared authority
-       order, then soft target shortfall. The control treats all failed constraints equally and
-       retries in the frozen candidate order.
-    3. Match candidate count, exact checks, retry cap, and CPU wall allowance. Prohibit source model,
-       family, answer labels, future outcomes, and exact utility from proposal-time features.
-    4. For every unit record selected proposal, legality, hard and binding outcomes, accepted
-       progress, retries, candidates consumed, certificate, work, and latency. Count no-candidate
-       abstention separately from failure.
-    5. Preregister positive only when hard violations remain zero, accepted progress or retry cost
-       improves with a positive paired lower bound, no family loses legal support, and harmful
-       selection does not increase. A completed null is valid.
-    6. Set priority_arbiter_ab_completed from row, budget, reducer, and manifest completeness. This
-       exact field is consumed by Exp6805.
-    7. Run focused tests, ruff, spec coverage, adversarial verification, artifact convention audit,
-       and verdict-row consistency lint.
-    8. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles; inference_substrate (deterministic CPU replay,
-       no LLM); duration_s; random_seed; reproducibility_checksum; source_artifact_sha256;
-       frozen_manifest; arm_definitions; feature_allowlist; feature_denylist; budget_match_receipt;
-       rows (every scenario-model-seed-arm unit); hard_violation_rate_by_arm;
-       binding_shortfall_by_arm; accepted_progress_by_arm; retry_cost_by_arm;
-       candidate_use_by_arm; certificate_completeness_by_arm; latency_by_arm;
-       harmful_selections_by_arm; paired_progress_delta; paired_retry_delta;
-       acceptance_gate_positive; priority_arbiter_ab_completed (exact downstream field);
-       gate_check_summary; verifier_is_oracle (false because exact outcomes evaluate after
-       selection); verdict_class (closed enum: positive | circular_positive | null | blocked |
-       disqualified | partial); and honest_verdict.
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6804_priority_arbiter_ab.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
-
